  "query_preview": "(Thursday through Sunday)...\nThe warming trend will continue through Thursday with high\ntemperatures on Thursday around 10 degrees above average for the\nmountains and deserts to 10 to 15 degrees above average for the\ncoast and valleys. High temperatures on Thursday will range from\nthe 80s near the coast to 105 to 110 for the Inland Empire with\n112 to 116 for the lower deserts. Low temperatures on Thursday \nwill be as much as 10 to 15 degrees above average for the \nmountains and inland valleys. Low temperatures for the coast and \nvalleys will be mostly in the 70s. There could be a large number \nof records for warmest low temperatures tied or broken on \nThursday and Friday.\n\nTemperatures will gradually cool for Friday through Sunday with\nhigh temperatures for Sunday around 5 degrees above average. High\ntemperatures on Sunday will range from around 80 near the coast to\nthe mid 90s to 103 for the Inland Empire with 108 to 112 for the\nlower deserts. \n\nThe HeatRisk is expected to peak on Thursday with major to extreme\nHeatRisk for the lower deserts, valleys, inland Orange County, and\nthe Santa Ana Mountains with moderate to major HeatRisk elsewhere\nexpected for the mountains above 7000 feet.",
